Z||000012||Seanh||11-09-2000||10:38 PM||||Anyone know of a good source to port and polish heads? Or a place to buy them already done? I am putting in a 3.4 after x-mas and need to do somthing with the heads. I am going to have the exhaust manifolds ported and TB and plenum bored to 56mm. <P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/seanhsig.gif">    <BR>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"If you smoke after sex, you're doing it way to fast".</I>||||reg||1
Z||000013||Shaun41178||11-10-2000||01:11 AM||||Ok you guys are only looking at the peak numbers.  Peak numbers don't mean jack in this dyno printout.  As you can see the peak occured when the car shifted to the next gear.  What you have to look at is the power curve throughout the mph range there.  Yea peak is only .2 but the increase is like at least 2 hp.  Look at the increase at about 37 mph.  I believe that is the biggest gain my car had.  That is about a 4 hp gain at 37 mph.  Follow the graph in second gear and you can tell that it is at least 2 hp increase all the way till it shifts to 3rd gear.  Look at the torque after the shift into second gear about 50 mph.  That appears to be about a 5 lb-ft increase and it is about 2 or so increase till 3rd gear.<P>Peak numbers dont' mean anything.  the power curve is what is important and as you can plainly see it increases hp and torque throughout the entire rpm/mph range.<P>If you don't think the ported TB is a good mod cause it only adds .2 peak hp according to this dyno printout then thats ok with me.  Besides this wasn't the $150 option but just the $75 ported TB.  A matched upper intake manifold probably would have been worth 1-2 more hp and torque throughout the range.<P>The reason why the hp and torque fell off in third gear is because I disconnected my TCC lockup switch to see what effect it has on the baseline and had nothing to do with the TB.<P>I hope this helps clarify some of the confusion.<P>------------------<BR>Shaun-Toledo OH, 85 GT<BR>3.2 With nitrous<BR>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178||||reg||1
Z||000014||88formula||11-10-2000||05:11 PM||||Seanh Go here  <A HREF="http://www.norrisracingtech.com/home.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.norrisracingtech.com/home.html</A>  They have the ported heads you are looking for.<P><p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 11-10-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||86se/lambo||11-13-2000||12:46 AM||||can you use a dremmel tool and do your own porting of the throttle body? anybody do this?||||reg||1
Z||000016||FIEROCIOUS||11-13-2000||12:50 AM||||I wouldn't use a dremel to inconsistant you might try a brake hone? you would need to find a bigger butterfly though.||||reg||1
Z||000017||1FST2M6||11-13-2000||08:48 AM||||You CAN use a dremel or air-drill for the intake pelenum but not the TB. it has to be a perfect circle so the new butterfly will seat properly and your idle won't do strange things. the pelenum MUST BE OFF THE CAR WHEN YOU START GRINDING ON IT!  there have been a few gimp kids bring thier rides to the shop cause "it just stoped" hours later you find out they "ported their intake" while it was on the car... "but dude i had a vacuum next to it the whole time" that doens't mean anything! you can do the pelenum but send the really important parts to a reputable shop. <P>------------------<BR>"Fondue forks for everybody"||||reg||1
Z||000018||HYPTNOTiSE||11-13-2000||11:06 AM||||Actually not sure if everyone knows this little fact about fiero TB's. They're actually elipitical in shape, they're not perfectly round. So when darrel does it, he makes them round and cuts a perfect throttle butterfly and installs it. ||||reg||1
Z||000019||1FST2M6||11-13-2000||11:19 AM||||learn somthing new everyday.. thats cool.. ||||reg||1
